ca-06053-bos-matter-66985.title:
a. Approve a new Funding Agreement with Edward and Kimberly Roth to fund the preparation of an Initial Study and Hydrogeologic Report and associated fees where the Base Budget is $50,662, the County Project Management/Contract Administration Fee is $7,600 (15% of the Base Budget), and the Project Contingency is $7,600 (15% of the Base Budget) for a not-to-exceed amount of $65,860, and term from execution to February 28, 2027;
b. Authorize the Director of Housing and Community Development or designee to execute the Funding Agreement with Edward and Kimberly Roth in the amount of $65,860 and three future amendments that do not significantly alter the scope of work and do not increase the Agreement’s amount by more than 10% ($6,586 each), bringing the total cumulative cost increase to $19,758 and potential aggregate not-to-exceed amount to $85,618, subject to review by County Counsel and the Auditor-Controller; and
c. Authorize the Director of Housing and Community Development or designee to execute the Professional Services Agreement with EMC Planning Group, Inc., in the amount of $58,261 and three future amendments to the Agreement that do not significantly alter the scope of work and do not increase the Agreement’s amount by more than 10% ($5,827 each) bringing the total cumulative cost increase to $17,479 and potential aggregate not-to-exceed amount to $75,739, subject to review by County Counsel and the Auditor-Controller.

ca-06053-bos-matter-67043.title:
a.  Approve Professional Services Agreement (PSA) with Moffatt & Nichol, a California Corporation, to provide professional design services for the Scenic Road Protection Structure Project in Carmel, California, County Project No. 450017, Request for Proposals (RFP) No. 10999, for an initial term of three years effective November 3, 2026 to November 2, 2029, with the option to extend the term for two additional one-year periods, for an amount not to exceed $1,605,057; 
b.  Authorize the Director of Public Works, Facilities and Parks (PWFP) or designee to extend the PSA beyond the anticipated five-year term of RFP No. 10999 with no change in the scope of work or increase to the dollar amount to allow continuity of services initiated during the anticipated five-year term of the PSA, subject to review and approval as to form by the Office of the County Counsel; and
c.  Authorize the Director of PWFP or designee to execute the PSA and up to three future amendments to the PSA where the amendments do not significantly alter the scope of work or increase the amount by more than 10% ($160,506) of the original approved PSA amount of $1,605,057 bringing the potential overall aggregate not to exceed amount to $1,765,563 subject to review and approval as to form by the Office of the County Counsel and as to fiscal provisions by the Auditor-Controller’s Office.

ca-06053-bos-matter-67050.title:
a.  Reappoint and approve a four-year employment agreement for the Monterey County Agricultural Commissioner and Sealer of Weights & Measures; 
b.   Authorize the Chair of the Board of Supervisors to execute the proposed employment agreement between the County of Monterey and the Monterey County Agricultural Commissioner; 
c.  Amend Personnel Policies and Practices Resolution (PPPR) Number 98-394 Appendix A and B to adjust the salary range of the Agricultural Commissioner classification effective February 6, 2027, as indicated in Attachment B; 
d.  Authorize subsequent annual adjustments of 2.5% for the Agricultural Commissioner classification, effective February 5, 2028, February 3, 2029, and February 2, 2030, consistent with the terms of the approved employment agreement; and,
e.  Direct the Human Resources Department and the Auditor-Controller’s Office to implement the changes in the Advantage Human Resources Management (HRM) System.
